<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guéréda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guéréda is a town in the Wadi Fira region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. It is the main centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tama-people">Tama people</a> and of the former sultanate of Dar Tama, which was set up in the surrounding hills by the 17th century and later fell under the influence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a>. The area was affected by the fighting and refugee movements of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> conflict in the 2000s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guereda.jpg" alt="Guéréda" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Korom10 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dignit%C3%A9_international.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
